rumc-city-whitehall-name = Port Whitehall
rumc-city-whitehall-desc = A great trading port on the coast of the sea. Half of the cargo of the world passes through it, and the duties here are lower than anywhere.
rumc-city-ironfall-name = Fort Ironfall
rumc-city-ironfall-desc = A fortified city of the gunsmiths. Arms are made and sold here, and the caravans go under guard.
rumc-city-eden-name = Academy City Eden
rumc-city-eden-desc = A city of scholars and mapmakers. They know what goes on in the world and gladly share the news.
rumc-city-corsair-name = Corsair Harbour
rumc-city-corsair-desc = A pirate harbour where nobody asks whose cargo it is. What no other place takes is bought and sold here.
rumc-city-frostgate-name = Frostgate
rumc-city-frostgate-desc = A fortress city on the trade ways. All the caravans pass through its gates, and its scribes know of every one of them.
rumc-city-sunreach-name = Sunreach
rumc-city-sunreach-desc = A city of the caravans. By day they trade spice and metal here, and by night what is not spoken of aloud.
rumc-city-dustwell-name = Dustwell
rumc-city-dustwell-desc = A mining town. Ore and powder go from here straight to the gunsmiths.
rumc-city-capeharbour-name = Cape Harbour
rumc-city-capeharbour-desc = A far port. The ships of the whole world meet at its quays.
rumc-city-greywater-name = Greywater
rumc-city-greywater-desc = A fishing city. The fishermen see every ship that goes by.

rumc-biome-ocean-name = Ocean
rumc-biome-ocean-desc = Open deep water. There is no land here, only sea routes: ships go along them from port to port, and storms are common.
rumc-biome-shallows-name = Shallows
rumc-biome-shallows-desc = Warm shallow water by the shore. Fish are caught and ports stand here, but big ships can run aground.
rumc-biome-ice-name = Ice waste
rumc-biome-ice-desc = Eternal ice and snow. Nobody lives here, and the way over the ice is long and dangerous.
rumc-biome-tundra-name = Tundra
rumc-biome-tundra-desc = A cold plain of frozen ground and sparse moss. Few people live here, and fewer roads run.
rumc-biome-taiga-name = Taiga
rumc-biome-taiga-desc = Cold forests of conifers. Much timber and fur, few people; caravans go along the rivers.
rumc-biome-forest-name = Forest
rumc-biome-forest-desc = Thick temperate forests. Good for hunters and woodcutters, but a wagon train goes slowly through a forest.
rumc-biome-plains-name = Plains
rumc-biome-plains-desc = Wide fields and meadows. The best land for roads and farms; the busiest cities stand here.
rumc-biome-desert-name = Desert
rumc-biome-desert-desc = Dry sand and stone. Water is dearer than gold, and caravans go from well to well.
rumc-biome-savanna-name = Savanna
rumc-biome-savanna-desc = A hot plain of dry grass and scattered trees. Easy to cross, but there is little water.
rumc-biome-jungle-name = Jungle
rumc-biome-jungle-desc = Hot and wet forests where everything grows too fast. There are almost no roads, but there are many rare herbs and much timber.
rumc-biome-mountains-name = Mountains
rumc-biome-mountains-desc = Cliffs and passes. Rich in ore, but they can be crossed only by a few roads.
rumc-biome-swamp-name = Swamp
rumc-biome-swamp-desc = Bogs and mist. There are no roads, and only the locals know the way through.


